  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p>This small Blaster Rifle has a short barrel and compact two-handed grip, making it look more like a long pistol than a rifle. Some Blaster Carbines, such as the E-5 used by <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/B1-Series_Battle_Droids\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"B1-Series Battle Droids\">B1-Series Battle Droids</a>, have a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Retractable_Stock\" title=\"Retractable Stock\">Retractable Stock</a>. A Blaster Carbine without a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Retractable_Stock\" title=\"Retractable Stock\">Retractable Stock</a> costs 850 credits (instead of 900 credits). </p><p>Because of its compact design, a Blaster Carbine can always be used to make an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Attack_of_Opportunity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Attack of Opportunity\">Attack of Opportunity</a>, even if its stock is not folded. A Blaster Carbine requires a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> to operate. After 50 shots, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> must be replaced. </p><p><b>Inaccurate:</b>&nbsp;This weapon cannot fire at targets at Long <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
    "textDescription": "",
